1
00:00:01,200 --> 00:00:03,640
I am famous high school
student detective,  Kudo Shinichi.

2
00:00:03,930 --> 00:00:06,110
One day when I went with my childhood
friend Ran to an amusement park...

3
00:00:06,270 --> 00:00:09,400
...I witnessed a scene of some men
in black involved in some suspicious deal.

4
00:00:09,710 --> 00:00:11,720
And then one of those men
made me take a drug.

5
00:00:11,950 --> 00:00:13,880
When I woke up,
my body had been shrunken.

6
00:00:14,560 --> 00:00:16,410
If they knew that Kudo
Shinichi was still alive...

7
00:00:16,490 --> 00:00:18,270
...they would bring harm
to all those around me.

8
00:00:18,830 --> 00:00:21,980
Naming myself Edogawa Conan, I look for
information on the Black Organization.

9
00:00:22,100 --> 00:00:23,850
The people who know my true identity are...

10
00:00:23,980 --> 00:00:26,880
Professor Agasa and my
classmate Haibara Ai.

11
00:00:27,070 --> 00:00:29,260
Her real name is Miyano Shiho.

12
00:00:29,550 --> 00:00:31,960
Her codename in
the Black Organization is Sherry.

13
00:00:32,220 --> 00:00:36,140
She developed the drug known as
Apoptoxin 4869 which made me small.

14
00:00:37,020 --> 00:00:40,250
In order to escape the organization
after they had killed her sister...

15
00:00:40,600 --> 00:00:43,740
...she took the drug herself.
And became Haibara Ai.

16
00:00:43,930 --> 00:00:45,470
She is now researching an antidote.

17
00:00:46,080 --> 00:00:51,050
But we only know that Apoptoxin 4869
can be suppressed with alcohol compounds...

18
00:00:51,360 --> 00:00:54,010
...returning our bodies to
their original form momentarily.

19
00:00:55,240 --> 00:00:57,160
I may be small but
my intellect is still as it was.

20
00:00:57,400 --> 00:01:00,030
There is always one truth!

21
00:01:04,380 --> 00:01:08,620
And this is the latest story.

22
00:01:27,050 --> 00:01:28,410
“Black Organization- Gin”
It stinks.

23
00:01:29,950 --> 00:01:32,120
“Black Organization- Vodka”
It stinks?

24
00:01:41,280 --> 00:01:46,780
It reeks of the scent of
the woman who betrayed us.

25
00:01:51,420 --> 00:01:54,780
I have a feeling that
we’ll meet her tonight.

26
00:01:56,910 --> 00:02:00,060
Sherry...you.

27
00:02:13,360 --> 00:02:17,520
Wow...What a beautiful hotel!

28
00:02:22,320 --> 00:02:24,360
“Edogawa Conan”

29
00:02:24,680 --> 00:02:29,480
Nice...There must be plenty of
famous people staying here.

30
00:02:29,820 --> 00:02:32,160
You can feel the presence of
Suzuki Conglomerate here, right?

31
00:02:32,640 --> 00:02:37,200
This is a splendid hotel, right? Ai?

32
00:02:37,320 --> 00:02:39,520
“Haibara Ai”

33
00:02:39,760 --> 00:02:45,310
“Ah! I want to stay here with Shinichi”
Weren’t you thinking about it?

34
00:02:45,800 --> 00:02:50,270
No, I wasn’t...I was only thinking
of staying with Conan.

35
00:02:50,800 --> 00:02:53,200
-Was it right, Conan?
-Eh...Yeah.

36
00:02:53,790 --> 00:02:55,920
They are both the same person though.

37
00:02:56,120 --> 00:02:59,850
It’s a million years too early
for this brat to be living in this hotel.

38
00:03:00,120 --> 00:03:02,600
That Sonoko...

39
00:03:03,340 --> 00:03:05,560
Oh? Where is Uncle Kogoro?

40
00:03:06,880 --> 00:03:08,720
About that…

41
00:03:09,150 --> 00:03:10,990
“Detective Mori Kogoro”
What? What? What?

42
00:03:11,230 --> 00:03:13,340
You can meet Miss Japanesque?!

43
00:03:19,610 --> 00:03:22,240
“Miss Japanesque Kotobuki Karen”

44
00:03:22,960 --> 00:03:26,780
Karen. You’re beautiful.

45
00:03:29,280 --> 00:03:32,060
Where? Where? Where? Where?
Where is it?

46
00:03:32,300 --> 00:03:34,490
The new hotel which belongs to Sonoko.

47
00:03:34,730 --> 00:03:38,560
They said the party is being broadcasted
live and attended by famous people.

48
00:03:38,800 --> 00:03:39,790
I see.

49
00:03:40,250 --> 00:03:41,610
When it comes to famous people…

50
00:03:41,770 --> 00:03:45,850
Then I, Mori Kogoro who
has solved many cases in the past.

51
00:03:46,410 --> 00:03:50,220
<i>Hey. Hey.
I was the one who solved them all.</i>

52
00:03:51,310 --> 00:03:53,960
It can’t be helped...I’ll have to go then.

53
00:03:54,830 --> 00:03:57,020
I’ll go change into my tuxedo.

54
00:03:57,600 --> 00:03:59,930
Wait dad!

55
00:04:00,190 --> 00:04:03,390
It isn’t my fault if Karen falls for me.

56
00:04:12,480 --> 00:04:14,860
No. No. I want to meet her.
I want to meet Karen.

57
00:04:14,970 --> 00:04:18,080
And so. He fell down
the stairs and broke his leg.

58
00:04:18,170 --> 00:04:24,090
No. No!
Karen…I need to meet her.

59
00:04:25,130 --> 00:04:26,750
He must be resting in
the hospital right now.

60
00:04:27,360 --> 00:04:29,930
And so...Ai and I are taking his place.

61
00:04:31,040 --> 00:04:32,590
We didn’t have time to change.

62
00:04:32,830 --> 00:04:35,800
-Is it alright if we came dressed like this?
-It’ll be fine.

63
00:04:35,920 --> 00:04:38,750
You look cute in anything you wear.
Let's go.

64
00:04:42,190 --> 00:04:44,090
Why did you have to come?

65
00:04:45,020 --> 00:04:46,000
Don’t you know?

66
00:04:46,400 --> 00:04:51,320
For a woman, she needs to look at
other women to improve herself.

67
00:04:51,960 --> 00:04:53,230
Huh?

68
00:04:58,560 --> 00:05:01,320
-Sonoko.
-We’ll be in your hands for today.

69
00:05:02,380 --> 00:05:05,390
This is Mimi, Miss Japanesque,
Karen’s sister.

70
00:05:05,680 --> 00:05:06,840
“Karen’s sister, Kotobuki Mimi”

71
00:05:06,960 --> 00:05:12,330
My sister had received
a letter threatening her.

72
00:05:19,950 --> 00:05:21,180
“My precious Karen…”

73
00:05:21,820 --> 00:05:23,400
“Congratulations on receiving the award”

74
00:05:23,850 --> 00:05:26,490
“Tonight, I will strike your heart…”

75
00:05:26,760 --> 00:05:28,730
“And make you my puppet”

76
00:05:29,500 --> 00:05:33,470
“Disobey me and you will DIE”

77
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:35,760
I was under the door just now.

78
00:05:36,080 --> 00:05:38,720
I have informed
several members of the staff.

79
00:05:40,320 --> 00:05:41,450
It smells sweet.

80
00:05:41,660 --> 00:05:42,960
That’s dangerous.

81
00:05:43,120 --> 00:05:45,660
-Let’s call the police immediately.
-That’s unnecessary.

82
00:05:48,600 --> 00:05:49,930
Look.

83
00:05:54,060 --> 00:05:55,720
Let him come at me if he wants to.

84
00:05:56,440 --> 00:05:59,870
I have worked so hard
to become Miss Japanesque.

85
00:06:01,150 --> 00:06:04,040
I won’t lose to a coward like this.

86
00:06:10,200 --> 00:06:13,400
-Did you just put in 10 times too much?
-I’m sorry.

87
00:06:14,430 --> 00:06:17,050
It may taste strange but it isn’t bad.

88
00:06:17,290 --> 00:06:20,320
-Just serve them as it is.
-Yes.

89
00:06:38,220 --> 00:06:42,140
-Here you go.
-Oh. It looks delicious.

90
00:06:42,280 --> 00:06:44,760
Here. Cake for the children.

91
00:06:44,920 --> 00:06:47,980
Even so, Karen must be a strong woman.

92
00:06:48,640 --> 00:06:52,300
But we don’t even know
which weirdo wrote that letter.

93
00:06:52,620 --> 00:06:56,920
Ran, go call
your husband, Shinichi Kudo.

94
00:06:57,000 --> 00:06:58,890
Eh!

95
00:06:59,520 --> 00:07:01,580
Ran...Please!

96
00:07:02,780 --> 00:07:04,000
Okay.

97
00:07:09,820 --> 00:07:12,000
It’s his mailbox again…

98
00:07:12,270 --> 00:07:17,290
Shinichi...Miss Japanesque, Karen
had received a threatening letter.

99
00:07:18,140 --> 00:07:19,960
If you can come…

100
00:07:20,220 --> 00:07:22,160
Your precious Ran is in trouble.

101
00:07:22,270 --> 00:07:24,700
Come to Bell Hotel immediately. |
Got it?

102
00:07:25,150 --> 00:07:27,400
Sonoko...Shinichi is
very busy, you know?

103
00:07:27,530 --> 00:07:29,980
If he doesn’t come because of this,
just dump him already!

104
00:07:30,060 --> 00:07:32,080
That man’s been missing
since forever.

105
00:07:33,400 --> 00:07:34,990
What will you do?

106
00:07:35,560 --> 00:07:38,320
You can give her a call,
you know...

107
00:07:39,720 --> 00:07:41,210
You’re right.

108
00:08:17,880 --> 00:08:19,080
Kudo.

109
00:08:19,310 --> 00:08:20,800
Haibara...

110
00:08:21,180 --> 00:08:22,910
That cake...

111
00:08:22,910 --> 00:08:25,110
Yes. That taste…

112
00:08:25,110 --> 00:08:26,720
The one you were made to drink…

113
00:08:26,720 --> 00:08:28,960
Baigar wine...it’s probably in the liquor.

114
00:08:32,410 --> 00:08:34,480
Haibara...hurry.

115
00:08:36,760 --> 00:08:40,800
My body feels hot.
It’s returning back to original form.

116
00:08:44,780 --> 00:08:46,960
Are you alright? Haibara...

117
00:08:47,200 --> 00:08:51,820
Sorry for having you break
into the girls’ changing room.

118
00:08:52,220 --> 00:08:53,710
What will we do now?

119
00:08:53,850 --> 00:08:56,430
If we transform back
into our original bodies.

120
00:08:56,960 --> 00:08:57,920
Haibara!

121
00:09:03,640 --> 00:09:05,600
Very well.
We’ll go with that, please.

122
00:09:07,770 --> 00:09:09,000
Hello there.

123
00:09:09,150 --> 00:09:11,310
Nice to meet you.

124
00:09:15,180 --> 00:09:16,910
I’m wearing white, you see.

125
00:09:17,450 --> 00:09:18,750
You go and change.

126
00:09:19,370 --> 00:09:21,520
Didn’t you say that
you were wearing black?

127
00:09:21,630 --> 00:09:23,680
The colour of the stage lights
made me change my mind.

128
00:09:24,240 --> 00:09:25,370
Hurry on now.

129
00:09:33,610 --> 00:09:34,590
"Runner-up Kyoumi Kawada"

130
00:09:34,680 --> 00:09:37,980
Take this off.
My tiara wouldn’t stand out.

131
00:09:38,640 --> 00:09:42,350
This is my mother’s momento.
I will never take this off.

132
00:09:42,670 --> 00:09:43,820
Karen, can you stop this already?

133
00:09:43,930 --> 00:09:47,080
Mr Miura.
You are the head of judges, right?

134
00:09:47,400 --> 00:09:50,090
Remove her from the list of runner-ups.

135
00:09:50,560 --> 00:09:51,760
Please.

136
00:09:52,860 --> 00:09:54,270
Can you take that off?

137
00:10:02,480 --> 00:10:04,510
Karen says that she wants
to stand closer to the front.

138
00:10:04,800 --> 00:10:06,750
She just wants
to stand out by herself.

139
00:10:06,910 --> 00:10:07,960
"Stage Director Shoichi Amano"

140
00:10:08,080 --> 00:10:09,020
We’ve another 10 minutes.

141
00:10:09,210 --> 00:10:10,880
Hurry and tell them
to change the lighting.

142
00:10:13,320 --> 00:10:16,810
Suzuki Conglomerate,
commemorating the opening of Bell Hotel…

143
00:10:17,200 --> 00:10:20,640
Will now begin the
Miss Japanesque Awards Ceremony.

144
00:10:26,350 --> 00:10:27,930
Conan and Ai are late…

145
00:10:28,250 --> 00:10:30,510
They are just playing around like kids.

146
00:10:30,700 --> 00:10:33,210
And now...two of the
Miss Japanesque runner-ups.

147
00:10:33,880 --> 00:10:37,480
Sumika Abe and Kyoumi Kawada.

148
00:11:01,930 --> 00:11:03,420
Thank you for waiting.

149
00:11:03,900 --> 00:11:09,040
And now, this year’s Miss Japanesque,
Kotobuki Karen!

150
00:11:09,150 --> 00:11:10,780
More tightly, Camera 3!

151
00:12:19,050 --> 00:12:22,520
Today is a day of beginning for me.

152
00:12:23,690 --> 00:12:26,320
I will definitely get
top spot in the world pageant.

153
00:12:27,210 --> 00:12:31,130
I believe that it is my duty to promote
the beauty of Japan to the world.

154
00:12:35,160 --> 00:12:40,010
From the bottom of my heart,
I wish to thank the people involved...

155
00:12:40,170 --> 00:12:41,450
Yes, this is Agasa.

156
00:12:41,660 --> 00:12:42,810
Shinichi?

157
00:12:46,540 --> 00:12:49,560
Trust me...I’ll come for you now.

158
00:12:50,270 --> 00:12:51,760
Professor?

159
00:12:52,010 --> 00:12:56,110
It’s Ai. She and Conan are lost
and I have to look for them.

160
00:12:56,480 --> 00:13:00,440
-Then, I’ll come…
-I’ll be fine. Stay here, Ran.

161
00:13:07,740 --> 00:13:09,530
Are you really Ai?

162
00:13:10,220 --> 00:13:12,540
Can you stop staring at me
like that, professor?

163
00:13:12,780 --> 00:13:16,810
No, I actually know about it.
But to see it with my eyes...

164
00:13:16,940 --> 00:13:20,040
It feels like “please to meet you”...

165
00:13:21,120 --> 00:13:24,670
Then, “it’s been a while” for me, right?

166
00:13:25,630 --> 00:13:27,420
Shinichi…

167
00:13:27,580 --> 00:13:29,070
You’re great help, professor.

168
00:13:29,560 --> 00:13:31,560
I almost had to crossdress.

169
00:13:32,040 --> 00:13:33,360
That’s bad...

170
00:13:33,470 --> 00:13:35,790
I wanted to see you crossdress.

171
00:13:36,490 --> 00:13:38,910
-It’ll look good on you, definitely.
-Shut up.

172
00:13:39,070 --> 00:13:41,760
That aside...what is going on, Shinichi?

173
00:13:42,030 --> 00:13:43,400
It’s just like that time...

174
00:13:43,580 --> 00:13:45,930
...when I accidentally drank
that wine in Baigar Province.

175
00:13:47,070 --> 00:13:49,710
I was able to return
to my original form...

176
00:13:50,200 --> 00:13:52,300
...thanks to the effects of
the wine’s compounds.

177
00:13:53,610 --> 00:13:56,810
That aside, we shouldn’t let Haibara
appear in front of many people.

178
00:13:57,080 --> 00:13:59,640
Now that she’s become like this.

179
00:14:00,220 --> 00:14:02,110
Take her back
to your place immediately.

180
00:14:05,150 --> 00:14:08,840
But Shinichi, wouldn’t that
be the same for you?

181
00:14:09,310 --> 00:14:11,080
I can’t go back yet.

182
00:14:11,290 --> 00:14:13,390
Are you going to see
your precious girlfriend?

183
00:14:13,790 --> 00:14:15,340
Fool.

184
00:14:15,710 --> 00:14:17,310
It’s that threatening letter.

185
00:14:17,930 --> 00:14:21,150
I’ll stay here until the party safely ends.

186
00:14:22,430 --> 00:14:25,000
We don’t know how long the effects
of the liquor in that cake will last.

187
00:14:26,140 --> 00:14:28,480
There’s no telling of when
you’ll revert back to being a child.

188
00:14:28,800 --> 00:14:29,820
I know.

189
00:14:30,120 --> 00:14:33,310
-If that’s so…
-No matter how dangerous it may be…

190
00:14:34,300 --> 00:14:37,020
It’s my nature as a detective...

191
00:14:37,440 --> 00:14:39,230
...not to run away
from a case in front of me.

192
00:14:41,400 --> 00:14:42,490
Take care of Haibara for me.

193
00:14:42,650 --> 00:14:44,570
My disguise.

194
00:14:46,490 --> 00:14:47,980
See you.

195
00:14:50,380 --> 00:14:52,670
Well then, let's go.

196
00:14:57,420 --> 00:14:59,050
First of all. Karen…

197
00:14:59,550 --> 00:15:02,970
How did you feel after winning?

198
00:15:04,300 --> 00:15:08,700
For the first 30 minutes,
Miss Japanesque will be on the stage.

199
00:15:09,420 --> 00:15:12,330
At that time, I will check
the layout of the hotel.

200
00:15:13,820 --> 00:15:15,790
For anything suspicious.

201
00:15:19,120 --> 00:15:22,940
Kotobuki Karen’s personal room
on the 20th floor is locked.

202
00:15:26,570 --> 00:15:28,510
In front is the head of judges’ room.

203
00:15:30,030 --> 00:15:32,300
What a simple human relationship.

204
00:15:39,820 --> 00:15:43,960
On the 10th floor are
the rooms of the runner-ups.

205
00:15:47,130 --> 00:15:51,280
Only staff members with
a pass can enter the stage.

206
00:15:53,310 --> 00:15:56,160
If the threatening letter was real...

207
00:15:56,520 --> 00:15:58,330
...where would the criminal attack from?

208
00:15:59,070 --> 00:16:03,480
Let’s give another round of
applause for Miss Japanesque.

209
00:16:07,000 --> 00:16:13,470
Finally, Miss Japanesque, Kotobuki Karen
will give a piano performance.

210
00:16:16,460 --> 00:16:18,490
Excuse me.
Would you like a drink?

211
00:16:19,080 --> 00:16:20,780
He’s nice.

212
00:16:20,910 --> 00:16:22,960
-Ah, juice please…
-Juice.

213
00:16:23,150 --> 00:16:26,040
-How about you, Ran?
-I’m fine.

214
00:16:26,510 --> 00:16:29,340
Conan and the others aren’t
back yet. I’ll go look for them.

215
00:16:43,240 --> 00:16:46,120
I guess that we’ve hit
the jackpot with this dress.

216
00:16:47,310 --> 00:16:51,200
If you do as I say, I will definitely
make you the world’s No.1.

217
00:16:52,140 --> 00:16:53,370
That’s delightful.

218
00:16:53,820 --> 00:16:54,700
Karen.

219
00:16:54,880 --> 00:16:57,450
Why did you change
the contents of your speech?

220
00:16:57,740 --> 00:16:59,520
Please do as I tell you.

221
00:16:59,690 --> 00:17:01,230
You’re so noisy.

222
00:17:01,470 --> 00:17:03,900
Don’t order me around just
because you’re my older sister.

223
00:17:04,650 --> 00:17:07,690
I’m letting you be
my manager out of pity.

224
00:17:10,760 --> 00:17:13,520
Karen. Please be
at standby at 8.45pm.

225
00:17:13,820 --> 00:17:15,370
I know that already.

226
00:17:20,460 --> 00:17:24,320
She acts like the queen, but
she couldn’t do anything by herself.

227
00:17:24,840 --> 00:17:26,700
She’s just like a puppet.

228
00:17:27,050 --> 00:17:28,280
Puppet?

229
00:17:29,400 --> 00:17:31,050
“Puppet”

230
00:17:32,030 --> 00:17:36,090
Just like that threatening letter,
I hope that she suffers...

231
00:17:37,310 --> 00:17:38,780
Kyoumi.

232
00:17:39,070 --> 00:17:42,090
You also feel that way, Amano, right?

233
00:17:42,380 --> 00:17:45,470
Like how many times she asked
for changes in the rehearsal.

234
00:17:45,630 --> 00:17:48,010
I’m just doing my job.

235
00:17:49,120 --> 00:17:51,000
The elevator’s here.

236
00:18:13,770 --> 00:18:15,200
Conan?

237
00:18:15,720 --> 00:18:17,020
Ai?

238
00:18:17,850 --> 00:18:19,260
Professor…

239
00:18:27,500 --> 00:18:28,890
Conan?

240
00:18:29,200 --> 00:18:30,760
Ai?

241
00:18:44,970 --> 00:18:46,320
Shinichi!

242
00:18:48,520 --> 00:18:49,820
Shinichi!

243
00:18:56,700 --> 00:18:59,450
Are you...Shinichi?

244
00:19:02,520 --> 00:19:04,700
I can tell by just looking at your hand.

245
00:19:19,930 --> 00:19:21,280
Yes.

246
00:19:25,240 --> 00:19:26,620
It’s me.

247
00:19:33,720 --> 00:19:35,820
Shinichi.

248
00:19:39,660 --> 00:19:42,170
I’ve finally found you.

249
00:19:44,170 --> 00:19:45,800
Finally…

250
00:19:47,820 --> 00:19:50,860
Fool...don’t cry.

251
00:19:51,580 --> 00:19:53,680
Where have you been all along?

252
00:19:55,600 --> 00:19:57,930
I’ve been so worried.

253
00:19:59,760 --> 00:20:01,710
I wanted to see you.

254
00:20:12,460 --> 00:20:13,870
Ran.

255
00:20:17,320 --> 00:20:18,520
Eh?

256
00:20:22,640 --> 00:20:25,480
You’ve gained weight...

257
00:20:25,760 --> 00:20:28,680
...since we last met.

258
00:20:29,440 --> 00:20:31,880
That’s not good.

259
00:20:32,960 --> 00:20:36,480
Now that you’ve said it.
My waist has recently…

260
00:20:36,920 --> 00:20:38,640
Is that something you say
after not seeing me for so long?

261
00:20:38,860 --> 00:20:41,300
Unbelievable.

262
00:20:42,420 --> 00:20:44,240
That’s so like you.

263
00:20:44,540 --> 00:20:47,340
Well. I forgive you.

264
00:20:48,860 --> 00:20:51,700
Since you heard
my voice message, right?

265
00:20:51,940 --> 00:20:55,680
Yes. And...I’m investigating
the hotel now.

266
00:20:55,960 --> 00:20:58,820
That said, why are you
wandering around?

267
00:21:00,480 --> 00:21:04,100
Conan and his friend, Ai are lost.

268
00:21:04,840 --> 00:21:07,640
Oh, If it’s about those brats...

269
00:21:07,820 --> 00:21:10,280
...the professor took them
home just now.

270
00:21:11,160 --> 00:21:12,760
Is that so?

271
00:21:14,300 --> 00:21:16,380
Then...

272
00:21:16,560 --> 00:21:18,380
I’ll go investigate with you.

273
00:21:18,720 --> 00:21:19,920
Eh?

274
00:21:20,740 --> 00:21:23,100
How old are you?

275
00:21:23,300 --> 00:21:26,960
-Sorry. But I’m working now.
-Do you have a girlfriend?

276
00:21:27,600 --> 00:21:29,620
Karen.

277
00:21:30,160 --> 00:21:32,780
Are you there? Answer me.

278
00:21:37,500 --> 00:21:39,640
-What is this ruckus about?
-Don’t act dumb.

279
00:21:39,960 --> 00:21:42,360
You’ve taken my sister
somewhere, right?

280
00:21:43,000 --> 00:21:45,260
Karen always says...

281
00:21:45,600 --> 00:21:48,760
<i>I’ll suffocate whenever
I’m with my gloomy sister.</i>

282
00:21:48,980 --> 00:21:50,440
What did you say?

283
00:21:51,200 --> 00:21:52,620
What’s wrong?

284
00:21:53,680 --> 00:21:55,000
You are?

285
00:21:55,420 --> 00:21:58,060
-Detectives.
-Detectives?

286
00:21:58,360 --> 00:22:01,600
I am Mori Kogoro’s assistant.

287
00:22:05,280 --> 00:22:08,600
Yes. We’re really my dad’s assistants.

288
00:22:10,940 --> 00:22:12,360
Is Karen missing?

289
00:22:12,580 --> 00:22:16,240
-This man’s taken her somewhere.
-I told you that I don’t know anything.

290
00:22:18,600 --> 00:22:20,280
That’s right.

291
00:22:21,480 --> 00:22:24,760
Let the detectives
prove my innocence.

292
00:22:25,180 --> 00:22:26,860
Please.

293
00:22:52,280 --> 00:22:54,440
She’s not in the room.

294
00:22:56,780 --> 00:23:00,360
Can we examine
Karen’s room just in case?

295
00:23:02,180 --> 00:23:03,960
Feel free to do so.

296
00:23:07,900 --> 00:23:10,260
Ran, check the bathroom.

297
00:23:17,680 --> 00:23:19,560
She’s not there.

298
00:23:27,860 --> 00:23:31,280
-When was Karen missing?
-A little while ago.

299
00:23:31,760 --> 00:23:34,680
She took a shower
after changing from her dress…

300
00:23:34,840 --> 00:23:36,080
When I wasn’t looking.

301
00:23:36,240 --> 00:23:38,700
-What dress would she be wearing next?
-It’s gone.

302
00:23:38,980 --> 00:23:42,140
-Together with belt for the dress.
-The belt for the dress?

303
00:23:42,320 --> 00:23:48,280
Karen will...in the end, rise up like
an angel from the stage basement.

304
00:23:48,540 --> 00:23:51,920
For that to happen,
she need that belt…

305
00:23:52,120 --> 00:23:55,440
In any case, I’m going to look for
my sister before the performance.

306
00:23:59,680 --> 00:24:01,060
That poor thing…

307
00:24:01,320 --> 00:24:05,880
With that meddling sister,
Karen’s nothing more than a puppet.

308
00:24:06,200 --> 00:24:07,920
A puppet?

309
00:24:08,520 --> 00:24:10,440
But she’s a professional.

310
00:24:10,780 --> 00:24:12,900
She will be there for the performance.

311
00:24:13,160 --> 00:24:15,560
There’s no cause for alarm.

312
00:24:21,420 --> 00:24:23,800
What will you do, Shinichi?

313
00:24:24,360 --> 00:24:26,040
We’ll look for Karen.

314
00:24:26,660 --> 00:24:28,440
Ran, go look at the ballroom.

315
00:24:29,000 --> 00:24:33,000
I cannot let people see me.

316
00:24:35,220 --> 00:24:36,700
I understand.

317
00:24:50,220 --> 00:24:51,540
Karen?

318
00:24:51,940 --> 00:24:53,560
I haven’t seen her.

319
00:24:54,360 --> 00:24:56,060
Thank you.

320
00:25:05,560 --> 00:25:08,340
-Where’s Karen?
-I haven’t found her yet.

321
00:25:18,220 --> 00:25:21,720
-Where’s this place?
-The stage basement.

322
00:25:22,900 --> 00:25:26,320
Karen will use this pulley, and
ascend to the stage from here.

323
00:25:26,760 --> 00:25:29,380
The head judge thought of it.

324
00:25:30,100 --> 00:25:33,780
Miura only thinks of
controlling my sister.

325
00:25:35,000 --> 00:25:36,580
I have to protect her.

326
00:25:37,500 --> 00:25:39,820
Controlling her...?

327
00:25:40,240 --> 00:25:41,760
Is Karen not with you?

328
00:25:42,040 --> 00:25:44,020
She didn’t come at all?

329
00:25:44,200 --> 00:25:46,780
It’s her usual selfishness again.

330
00:25:47,660 --> 00:25:49,200
Another 15 minutes
till the performance.

331
00:25:49,520 --> 00:25:51,940
She’ll probably appear
at the last minute.

332
00:26:08,240 --> 00:26:10,780
I’ll go there.
You can look there.

333
00:26:18,800 --> 00:26:20,060
What’s his problem?

334
00:26:20,280 --> 00:26:22,680
He can at least tell me his age.

335
00:26:36,840 --> 00:26:39,660
Karen is on standby
at the stage basement.

336
00:26:40,220 --> 00:26:42,560
She’s finally here.

337
00:27:01,520 --> 00:27:04,000
Yes. Yes.

338
00:27:05,580 --> 00:27:07,940
Thank goodness.

339
00:27:08,300 --> 00:27:11,800
Sorry for the trouble.
I’m counting on you.

340
00:27:12,460 --> 00:27:16,420
That was stage director, Amano.
She’s on standby.

341
00:27:17,400 --> 00:27:19,900
She’s probably harassing me.

342
00:27:20,700 --> 00:27:23,220
Thank you for helping look for her.

343
00:27:27,960 --> 00:27:30,920
Well then...
Thank you for waiting.

344
00:27:31,360 --> 00:27:36,980
Miss Japanesque.
Karen Kotobuki’s piano recital!

345
00:27:54,600 --> 00:27:56,700
You are late.

346
00:27:56,920 --> 00:27:58,460
A little.

347
00:28:44,100 --> 00:28:46,480
What’s that?

348
00:28:48,820 --> 00:28:50,680
That’s not part of the performance.

349
00:28:51,060 --> 00:28:53,520
-Did you do this?
-I don’t know.

350
00:28:53,660 --> 00:28:56,580
-That’s disgusting.
-She’s like a real puppet.

351
00:29:01,180 --> 00:29:03,100
What’s going on?

352
00:29:12,600 --> 00:29:14,640
She’s dead...

353
00:29:14,760 --> 00:29:16,520
Cut the cameras!

354
00:29:21,240 --> 00:29:23,420
Switch to commercials!
Commercials!

355
00:29:23,730 --> 00:29:24,270
Professor.

356
00:29:24,350 --> 00:29:25,710
Sorry, Shinichi.

357
00:29:25,710 --> 00:29:26,960
While I looked away...Ai…

358
00:29:26,960 --> 00:29:29,800
Listen. Don’t let anyone out
no matter what. Got it?

359
00:29:29,980 --> 00:29:32,280
No. Nobody may leave.

360
00:29:32,500 --> 00:29:34,860
-No!~
-Shinichi?

361
00:29:38,380 --> 00:29:40,020
Why did you come back?

362
00:29:40,420 --> 00:29:42,380
To retrieve that cake.

363
00:29:42,860 --> 00:29:45,660
If I analyse the contents,
then perhaps…

364
00:29:47,620 --> 00:29:50,920
-What are you doing?
-It’s a live broadcast on television.

365
00:29:51,180 --> 00:29:54,180
The viewership of this event
is likely about 20%.

366
00:29:54,580 --> 00:29:55,900
There’s a one out of 5 chance that...

367
00:29:56,160 --> 00:29:58,980
...the Black Organization
will learn of your whereabouts.

368
00:29:59,500 --> 00:30:02,540
In any case, get out of here
as soon as you can.

369
00:30:04,600 --> 00:30:06,360
No.

370
00:30:06,760 --> 00:30:09,080
I can’t let this chance slip away.

371
00:30:10,420 --> 00:30:14,180
How long do you plan to stay as a kid?

372
00:30:15,100 --> 00:30:17,340
Don’t you want to return
to being Shinichi Kudo?

373
00:30:18,820 --> 00:30:20,700
Shinichi...

374
00:30:22,140 --> 00:30:24,040
What are you doing?

375
00:30:31,280 --> 00:30:33,160
That’s none of your business.

376
00:30:34,380 --> 00:30:36,900
Wait!
What did you mean by that?

377
00:30:37,260 --> 00:30:40,620
Did you know how long
Ran had been waiting for you?

378
00:30:41,000 --> 00:30:44,600
And then you finally turn up
with another woman.

379
00:30:45,420 --> 00:30:49,040
Help. Somebody help me!

380
00:30:49,220 --> 00:30:52,360
Anyways, there’s no time
for explanations.

381
00:30:53,840 --> 00:30:56,620
Understood?
Hurry and get out of here.

382
00:31:04,480 --> 00:31:06,620
What’s with him?

383
00:31:09,060 --> 00:31:12,240
She...looks like someone.

384
00:31:32,620 --> 00:31:36,160
I missed you...Sherry.

385
00:31:47,800 --> 00:31:52,120
As usual, keep my involvement
in this investigation a secret.

386
00:31:52,460 --> 00:31:55,020
I wouldn’t mind if you said so.

387
00:31:55,940 --> 00:32:02,080
The criminal tied the victim’s limbs
and waist with strings.

388
00:32:02,280 --> 00:32:05,040
The strings were cut and…she fell.

389
00:32:06,020 --> 00:32:07,940
She was stabbed to death.

390
00:32:08,740 --> 00:32:11,580
Yes. Most likely.

391
00:32:12,660 --> 00:32:15,700
The victim had received
a threatening letter beforehand.

392
00:32:15,920 --> 00:32:19,540
This knife...she carried it
around for self defense.

393
00:32:19,740 --> 00:32:21,060
Inspector.

394
00:32:21,620 --> 00:32:23,460
The threatening letter.

395
00:32:25,100 --> 00:32:30,200
<i>Tonight, I will strike your heart,
And make you my puppet.</i>

396
00:32:30,460 --> 00:32:36,460
Her body was hung up just like a puppet.

397
00:32:36,640 --> 00:32:38,340
<i>“I will strike your heart…”</i>
means that...

398
00:32:38,520 --> 00:32:40,680
...she got stabbed in
the heart with a knife.

399
00:32:41,060 --> 00:32:45,080
This murder happened
just as the letter stated.

400
00:32:46,400 --> 00:32:47,620
Based on the report
from forensics...

401
00:32:47,740 --> 00:32:51,220
...the time of death is said to be
in between 8.30pm to 9pm.

402
00:32:52,000 --> 00:32:56,700
She wasn’t in the stage
basement at around 8.45pm.

403
00:32:57,560 --> 00:33:00,280
Excuse me Inspector.
I’ve brought him here.

404
00:33:01,380 --> 00:33:05,520
You were the last person
to see the victim alive, correct?

405
00:33:05,840 --> 00:33:08,340
Yes! It was 3 minutes
before the performance.

406
00:33:08,800 --> 00:33:11,000
From the top of the stage.

407
00:33:16,740 --> 00:33:19,660
Karen, the performance
will start soon.

408
00:33:19,940 --> 00:33:22,060
Are you ready?

409
00:33:23,140 --> 00:33:26,020
You started the performance
without her responding?

410
00:33:26,240 --> 00:33:29,040
It’s not unusual that
Karen doesn’t respond.

411
00:33:29,460 --> 00:33:31,660
Who would think that she’s dead?

412
00:33:31,820 --> 00:33:35,840
The time of the murder was...

413
00:33:35,960 --> 00:33:38,940
...between 8.45pm to 8.57pm.

414
00:33:39,320 --> 00:33:40,960
In a 12-minute timespan.

415
00:33:41,240 --> 00:33:44,920
And the person without an alibi within
this timespan would be the criminal.

416
00:33:45,600 --> 00:33:50,320
Even so, that is
a terrible way of killing someone.

417
00:33:52,800 --> 00:33:55,200
Excuse me.

418
00:33:56,060 --> 00:33:58,380
-Yes.
-Shinichi?

419
00:33:58,980 --> 00:33:59,720
Yes.

420
00:34:00,020 --> 00:34:02,560
Ai wouldn’t go home with me.

421
00:34:11,200 --> 00:34:13,000
Haibara.

422
00:34:14,580 --> 00:34:17,140
Even when we ate different amounts.

423
00:34:17,400 --> 00:34:20,880
The symptoms appeared
at the same time.

424
00:34:22,680 --> 00:34:25,760
Gender difference
may have been a factor.

425
00:34:26,740 --> 00:34:29,780
I need a sample no matter what.

426
00:34:33,660 --> 00:34:36,120
Hurry and leave!

427
00:34:36,620 --> 00:34:40,880
Even when you tell me that there’s
a 1 in 5 chance that I’ll be in danger…

428
00:34:42,480 --> 00:34:45,300
There’s a 4 out of 5 chance
that I’ll be safe.

429
00:34:46,860 --> 00:34:49,380
We’re in this together.

430
00:34:49,800 --> 00:34:51,580
We escape together…

431
00:34:51,940 --> 00:34:54,040
And investigate together.

432
00:34:55,380 --> 00:34:57,360
There’s no other way.

433
00:35:03,060 --> 00:35:05,360
-Ran.
-Sorry.

434
00:35:07,760 --> 00:35:11,780
The professor has the car ready
and told me to call you.

435
00:35:16,820 --> 00:35:18,780
Haibara.

436
00:35:24,380 --> 00:35:25,740
Ran.

437
00:35:26,060 --> 00:35:29,380
I’ll explain it later.
It’s an emergency.

438
00:35:30,120 --> 00:35:33,440
I’m sorry, but could you
take her to the professor?

439
00:35:34,160 --> 00:35:36,060
Please.

440
00:35:41,640 --> 00:35:43,480
I understand.

441
00:35:46,500 --> 00:35:49,780
Can I at least...have your name?

442
00:35:54,780 --> 00:35:56,760
You don’t have to…

443
00:35:57,060 --> 00:35:59,300
You have your reasons, right?

444
00:35:59,540 --> 00:36:04,760
-Her name is...Hai...
-Hairi.

445
00:36:05,720 --> 00:36:07,520
I’m half Japanese.

446
00:36:07,840 --> 00:36:09,300
Please to meet you.

447
00:36:09,760 --> 00:36:12,180
I’m Ran Mori.

448
00:36:15,660 --> 00:36:18,300
Hmm...

449
00:36:18,900 --> 00:36:22,140
Have I seen you before?

450
00:36:22,860 --> 00:36:26,220
It’s like I’ve known you from somewhere.

451
00:36:27,500 --> 00:36:29,300
Really?

452
00:36:30,280 --> 00:36:32,520
I’ve never met you before.

453
00:36:35,180 --> 00:36:37,260
I guess so.

454
00:36:38,860 --> 00:36:43,540
Well then, see you later...Shinichi.

455
00:36:59,080 --> 00:37:01,640
The professor’s car is that way.

456
00:37:02,200 --> 00:37:03,840
Let’s go.

457
00:37:16,680 --> 00:37:18,420
What's wrong?

458
00:37:31,660 --> 00:37:33,920
Who was that man?

459
00:37:46,080 --> 00:37:48,040
Professor.

460
00:37:48,300 --> 00:37:49,940
You’re still here…

461
00:37:50,280 --> 00:37:52,940
Someone was going to
attack Hairi with a knife.

462
00:37:56,520 --> 00:37:58,420
She protected me.

463
00:37:59,180 --> 00:38:00,700
Come here.

464
00:38:10,760 --> 00:38:12,640
It’s them?

465
00:38:14,440 --> 00:38:16,260
We’re already surrounded.

466
00:38:18,400 --> 00:38:21,700
I can’t let them see the professor
and her, together with us.

467
00:38:22,620 --> 00:38:25,200
And involve the two in our mess.

468
00:38:32,500 --> 00:38:38,400
By losing your knife,
you lose your life.

469
00:38:38,760 --> 00:38:41,640
So...what do we do now?

470
00:38:43,420 --> 00:38:45,720
They are trapped here.

471
00:38:46,140 --> 00:38:48,420
There’s no need to hurry.

472
00:38:49,760 --> 00:38:52,880
It would be fun to corner them slowly.

473
00:38:54,020 --> 00:38:56,560
I see you, Sherry...

474
00:38:57,020 --> 00:39:00,020
Your back shivering in fear.

475
00:39:05,100 --> 00:39:06,680
Haibara.

476
00:39:08,900 --> 00:39:10,460
I feel them.

477
00:39:11,360 --> 00:39:13,320
Their presence.

478
00:39:14,140 --> 00:39:16,260
They are near.

479
00:39:22,080 --> 00:39:24,920
Who is she?

480
00:39:27,680 --> 00:39:30,600
You know her, professor?

481
00:39:34,860 --> 00:39:38,000
I’ve heard that he uses an assistant.

482
00:39:38,360 --> 00:39:40,660
That must be her.

483
00:39:41,340 --> 00:39:45,160
He has an assistant. Yet he hasn’t
told me anything about her.

484
00:39:46,360 --> 00:39:48,040
And...

485
00:39:48,280 --> 00:39:52,260
He was talking to her with such
an expression in his face.

486
00:39:53,260 --> 00:39:56,660
It’s the first time
I’ve seen his face like that.

487
00:39:59,440 --> 00:40:04,240
It’s like Shinichi has became
a stranger to me.

488
00:40:04,600 --> 00:40:07,940
Shinichi is Shinichi, no matter what.

489
00:40:08,120 --> 00:40:09,680
He hasn’t changed.

490
00:40:10,040 --> 00:40:13,280
What would he do
if you do not trust him?

491
00:40:16,340 --> 00:40:19,640
I am already under
the organization’s crosshairs.

492
00:40:20,360 --> 00:40:23,800
All that’s left is for them to pull the trigger.

493
00:40:27,420 --> 00:40:31,320
It’s not like you to be all weak like that.

494
00:40:33,100 --> 00:40:37,140
At least, you’ll be safe with the police around.

495
00:40:38,360 --> 00:40:42,700
After that, I’ll protect you…

496
00:40:44,160 --> 00:40:46,600
You...

497
00:40:47,020 --> 00:40:49,060
...and also Ran.

498
00:40:51,140 --> 00:40:53,260
Can I ask for something?

499
00:40:56,960 --> 00:41:01,840
If I am close to danger,
don’t hesitate to leave me behind.

500
00:41:03,280 --> 00:41:06,700
Fool. Are you sleeptalking?

501
00:41:08,620 --> 00:41:12,220
A detective never
gets rid of his evidence...

502
00:41:12,620 --> 00:41:17,900
...even if it gets in
the way of his reasoning.

503
00:41:19,300 --> 00:41:24,160
I’ll add it into my reasoning and
hold unto it until I solve the case.

504
00:41:24,500 --> 00:41:26,360
Rest assured.

505
00:41:27,140 --> 00:41:28,340
Kudo.

506
00:41:28,520 --> 00:41:30,440
There are no fingerprints
on the knife...

507
00:41:30,800 --> 00:41:33,940
And we’ve gathered
everyone without an alibi.

508
00:41:34,380 --> 00:41:36,040
Understood.

509
00:41:37,640 --> 00:41:39,700
Who is this lady?

510
00:41:40,380 --> 00:41:43,600
Ah...! She’s my assistant.

511
00:41:46,660 --> 00:41:50,520
Then, from 8.45pm to 3 minutes
before the performance.

512
00:41:51,040 --> 00:41:53,960
Between those 12 minutes.

513
00:41:54,420 --> 00:41:58,540
Please tell us where and what
you were doing at that time.

514
00:41:59,620 --> 00:42:01,540
Starting with you.

515
00:42:02,180 --> 00:42:04,440
I was looking for my sister.

516
00:42:04,680 --> 00:42:07,500
And who can verify that?

517
00:42:09,300 --> 00:42:13,380
You were Karen’s manager…

518
00:42:15,520 --> 00:42:18,320
But I heard that your relationship
with her was bad.

519
00:42:18,560 --> 00:42:20,960
That was for her own good.

520
00:42:21,420 --> 00:42:24,860
-You...
-I was in my room all along.

521
00:42:25,840 --> 00:42:28,220
I had a phone call
with a business partner.

522
00:42:29,720 --> 00:42:31,980
You can confirm it with him.

523
00:42:32,500 --> 00:42:35,100
It’s possible that
he’s your accomplice.

524
00:42:36,300 --> 00:42:37,720
That doesn’t count as an alibi.

525
00:42:38,000 --> 00:42:41,820
And you are obsessed with Karen…

526
00:42:42,140 --> 00:42:47,700
But she neglected you and
you hated her at the same time.

527
00:42:47,960 --> 00:42:49,800
What did you say?

528
00:42:50,540 --> 00:42:52,880
Runner-up Miss Japanesque,
Abe Sumika...

529
00:42:53,420 --> 00:42:58,240
-Where were you?
-I was in Kyoumi’s room all along.

530
00:43:01,080 --> 00:43:05,740
Both of you thought ill of Karen.

531
00:43:06,740 --> 00:43:11,740
And should Karen disappear,
the person who gains the most is...

532
00:43:12,000 --> 00:43:14,420
...either one of you runner-ups.

533
00:43:15,280 --> 00:43:20,340
There’s a possibility that both of you
could have conspired to murder Karen.

534
00:43:22,300 --> 00:43:26,160
Stage director, Shoichi Amano.

535
00:43:26,740 --> 00:43:30,740
At 8.45pm, I was with
the both of them…

536
00:43:30,900 --> 00:43:33,240
I went to the stage basement
to see if she was there.

537
00:43:33,460 --> 00:43:36,320
And then I went to back
to tuning the equipment.

538
00:43:36,840 --> 00:43:40,480
I went to check if she was in
the basement several times, but…

539
00:43:40,700 --> 00:43:42,400
In other words…

540
00:43:42,780 --> 00:43:44,980
Your alibi isn’t perfect.

541
00:43:45,260 --> 00:43:50,260
Well. But why would I kill Karen?

542
00:43:50,440 --> 00:43:53,060
Don’t underestimate the police.

543
00:43:54,280 --> 00:43:58,060
You were her ex-lover.

544
00:43:58,480 --> 00:44:03,620
You were both in the theatre group
and saw the same dream, but…

545
00:44:03,820 --> 00:44:07,760
Now...look at how different
the two of you have become.

546
00:44:08,080 --> 00:44:10,320
I was happy with her success.

547
00:44:10,940 --> 00:44:12,840
That’s the truth.

548
00:44:19,060 --> 00:44:20,780
Is she there?

549
00:44:21,540 --> 00:44:25,820
No, not yet.
Not anywhere.

550
00:44:27,080 --> 00:44:29,280
Get ready.

551
00:44:30,060 --> 00:44:34,500
When the cops pull out,
that is when...

552
00:44:34,680 --> 00:44:37,140
...the hunt begins.

553
00:44:45,500 --> 00:44:47,920
What is this feeling?

554
00:44:50,380 --> 00:44:54,240
There’s something different
from when I came in before.

555
00:44:59,720 --> 00:45:03,320
And there is another
thing that feels off.

556
00:45:03,560 --> 00:45:05,340
<i>And I will make you my puppet...</i>

557
00:45:05,780 --> 00:45:07,080
Was it your idea?

558
00:45:07,240 --> 00:45:08,860
Like a puppet.

559
00:45:09,040 --> 00:45:11,240
What’s going on?

560
00:45:13,560 --> 00:45:15,440
There’s still something
I don’t understand.

561
00:45:15,760 --> 00:45:17,660
Take a look at this.

562
00:45:23,660 --> 00:45:28,000
This bloodtrail continues from
the entrance to the pulley.

563
00:45:31,180 --> 00:45:32,680
Inspector Megure.

564
00:45:33,020 --> 00:45:36,000
Please confirm whether
this is the victim’s blood.

565
00:45:36,560 --> 00:45:38,140
Alright.

566
00:45:40,620 --> 00:45:43,260
If this bloodstain is hers…

567
00:45:43,720 --> 00:45:47,240
She may have been murdered
elsewhere and then moved here.

568
00:45:48,200 --> 00:45:50,660
Why go through all that trouble?

569
00:45:51,840 --> 00:45:56,320
The first explanation is that...

570
00:45:56,760 --> 00:46:00,000
...it is too risky for
the criminal to kill her here.

571
00:46:00,740 --> 00:46:03,500
There’s no telling when a staff,
looking for Karen would appear.

572
00:46:03,900 --> 00:46:05,020
That said…

573
00:46:05,280 --> 00:46:08,420
He could have killed her in another
location and brought her here...

574
00:46:08,820 --> 00:46:12,620
...for the sake of the puppet show
over a short period of time.

575
00:46:14,420 --> 00:46:16,480
The second explanation?

576
00:46:17,120 --> 00:46:20,440
To hide the true murder scene.

577
00:46:23,920 --> 00:46:25,420
What's wrong?

578
00:46:25,740 --> 00:46:27,000
Nothing…

579
00:46:27,400 --> 00:46:29,840
Something’s wrong.

580
00:46:31,120 --> 00:46:32,880
Let’s go.

581
00:46:36,300 --> 00:46:39,420
Here’s the key to Karen’s room.

582
00:46:41,220 --> 00:46:43,260
What about the keys
to the other rooms?

583
00:46:43,700 --> 00:46:48,260
The rooms that were rented out,
were to Miura, Sumika and Kyoumi.

584
00:46:48,540 --> 00:46:51,080
The other keys are strictly
managed by the hotel.

585
00:46:51,360 --> 00:46:54,380
I see. Thank you.

586
00:46:58,900 --> 00:47:00,760
What was that?

587
00:47:02,460 --> 00:47:03,880
It can’t be helped.

588
00:47:05,060 --> 00:47:09,900
Shinichi cannot see anything else
when he’s on a case,

589
00:47:10,480 --> 00:47:11,720
Ran…

590
00:47:11,920 --> 00:47:14,240
Kindness is not just about being able
to understand others’ feelings.

591
00:47:14,480 --> 00:47:16,940
You also need to learn
when to be selfish.

592
00:47:19,140 --> 00:47:21,040
I’ll be fine.

593
00:47:22,060 --> 00:47:25,840
When the case is over,
I’ll talk to Shinichi properly.

594
00:47:26,800 --> 00:47:29,240
Please do not worry.

595
00:47:33,580 --> 00:47:36,400
I understand. Let’s go.

596
00:47:42,420 --> 00:47:45,380
But what was that about?

597
00:47:46,320 --> 00:47:49,580
Just now...

598
00:48:08,600 --> 00:48:10,020
Haibara.

599
00:48:10,880 --> 00:48:12,980
Don’t wander around
the hotel by yourself.

600
00:48:13,580 --> 00:48:16,160
Is it the time to be
worrying about me?

601
00:48:20,640 --> 00:48:24,840
She’s suffering with me around.

602
00:48:26,320 --> 00:48:29,420
She’s doing her best
to act as it isn’t.

603
00:48:30,240 --> 00:48:31,980
You know that, right?

604
00:48:33,620 --> 00:48:38,720
I don’t know how long
I’ll remain like this.

605
00:48:41,240 --> 00:48:46,120
Being kind to her now, only
makes separating more painful.

606
00:48:48,900 --> 00:48:51,520
What happens when
we return to a kid’s body?

607
00:48:53,220 --> 00:48:56,000
What if I cannot find a cure?

608
00:48:58,440 --> 00:49:01,460
Will we be classmates forever?

609
00:49:04,340 --> 00:49:07,020
Will we be able to
live normally forever?

610
00:49:09,380 --> 00:49:11,520
Forever…

611
00:49:12,700 --> 00:49:14,400
Haibara?

612
00:49:17,620 --> 00:49:19,760
It’ll be fine.

613
00:49:20,200 --> 00:49:23,660
If we don’t find the cure,
after 10 years, you’ll be 17.

614
00:49:24,420 --> 00:49:26,980
And Ran will be 27.

615
00:49:28,240 --> 00:49:30,520
Both of you will no longer
be children by then.

616
00:49:31,340 --> 00:49:35,560
I bet that you two will overcome
the age gap and fall in love.

617
00:49:37,440 --> 00:49:39,480
So don’t worry.

618
00:49:40,060 --> 00:49:41,780
Fool!

619
00:49:43,640 --> 00:49:46,780
How would you know
what would happen by then?

620
00:49:48,080 --> 00:49:53,240
I wouldn’t know but
I’m not giving up on hope.

621
00:49:55,080 --> 00:49:58,940
I’ll definitely get my body back...

622
00:49:59,300 --> 00:50:02,060
...and destroy those
Black Organization bastards.

623
00:50:02,500 --> 00:50:07,480
You want to avenge
your sister too, right?

624
00:50:13,220 --> 00:50:15,000
You’re right.

625
00:50:28,420 --> 00:50:33,540
The criminal hung the body,
even when it put him at risk.

626
00:50:41,900 --> 00:50:43,500
What is it?

627
00:50:44,020 --> 00:50:46,040
What bothers me?

628
00:50:53,400 --> 00:50:55,200
Damn...

629
00:50:55,700 --> 00:50:57,500
At a time like this.

630
00:51:00,340 --> 00:51:03,180
I’ve borrowed it.
The footage from just now.

631
00:51:03,640 --> 00:51:05,460
Let’s see it.

632
00:51:13,000 --> 00:51:14,420
This is it.

633
00:51:14,820 --> 00:51:16,900
That has been bothering me.

634
00:51:18,860 --> 00:51:23,540
But at that time, the five...

635
00:51:27,080 --> 00:51:29,220
Kudo?

636
00:51:41,040 --> 00:51:43,500
I see.

637
00:51:44,200 --> 00:51:48,500
That is probably why
the criminal did that to the body.

638
00:51:58,360 --> 00:51:59,860
On top of that…

639
00:52:00,080 --> 00:52:04,420
I now understand the other thing
that was bothering me.

640
00:52:06,040 --> 00:52:10,380
But there was another thing
which I didn’t understand.

641
00:52:11,500 --> 00:52:14,580
Damn!
I’m running out of time.

642
00:52:19,400 --> 00:52:21,220
Shinichi.

643
00:52:21,960 --> 00:52:26,400
-What’s wrong?
-Nothing.

644
00:52:27,180 --> 00:52:29,440
How can it be nothing?

645
00:52:31,440 --> 00:52:32,940
Why?

646
00:52:33,420 --> 00:52:36,560
Why wouldn’t you tell me?

647
00:52:39,900 --> 00:52:41,460
Ran.

648
00:52:51,680 --> 00:52:54,600
<i>I cannot turn back
into Conan in front of Ran.</i>

649
00:52:55,060 --> 00:53:00,240
<i>I need to do something
and solve this case.</i>

650
00:53:04,420 --> 00:53:06,640
I know who the criminal is.

651
00:53:07,380 --> 00:53:10,320
Gather everyone.

652
00:53:10,960 --> 00:53:13,120
Shinichi.

653
00:53:18,020 --> 00:53:20,040
I understand.

654
00:53:20,520 --> 00:53:22,540
I’ll go.

655
00:53:28,320 --> 00:53:34,960
Until you tell me everything,
I’ll wait for you.

656
00:53:37,440 --> 00:53:40,080
Because I believe in you.

657
00:53:52,100 --> 00:53:53,800
Ran.

658
00:54:05,920 --> 00:54:08,960
It’s over once you
transform in front of her.

659
00:54:09,400 --> 00:54:10,960
Yeah.

660
00:54:11,440 --> 00:54:14,240
That is why I need
to settle the case now.

661
00:54:20,380 --> 00:54:23,420
You know the criminal?
Really?

662
00:54:23,940 --> 00:54:25,540
Yes.

663
00:54:31,540 --> 00:54:37,060
The criminal who hung
the body on the stage...

664
00:54:37,840 --> 00:54:40,900
...wanted to show off
the murder in a reckless way.

665
00:54:41,920 --> 00:54:47,960
This murder happened just as
it was written in the threatening letter.

666
00:54:51,480 --> 00:54:53,660
Smell this.

667
00:54:59,400 --> 00:55:01,640
-This.
-Yes.

668
00:55:01,960 --> 00:55:04,000
The smell of a cigar.

669
00:55:06,840 --> 00:55:09,140
This threatening letter has...

670
00:55:09,480 --> 00:55:15,060
...the special sweet smell
of the cigar you smoke.

671
00:55:16,100 --> 00:55:18,200
Daigo Miura.

672
00:55:18,520 --> 00:55:21,700
Eh? No way.
Unbelievable.

673
00:55:22,100 --> 00:55:25,660
You may not notice
since you’re the smoker...

674
00:55:26,080 --> 00:55:28,040
...and your nose
is used to the smell.

675
00:55:32,680 --> 00:55:35,060
It was me.

676
00:55:37,180 --> 00:55:39,220
Once she became
Miss Japanesque...

677
00:55:39,460 --> 00:55:42,580
...Karen began to distance
herself from me.

678
00:55:44,020 --> 00:55:46,880
She had only been using me.

679
00:55:49,920 --> 00:55:53,380
But I wrote that!

680
00:55:54,000 --> 00:55:55,260
I didn’t kill her!

681
00:55:55,420 --> 00:55:56,960
Explain yourself
at the police station.

682
00:55:57,240 --> 00:55:59,420
Inspector Megure.

683
00:56:03,500 --> 00:56:05,280
Daigo Miura.

684
00:56:05,780 --> 00:56:09,900
You are under arrest for
the murder of Kotobuki Karen.

685
00:56:10,760 --> 00:56:14,160
Wait. I didn’t kill her.
It’s true.

686
00:56:14,340 --> 00:56:17,560
It wasn’t me! Hey. wait!

687
00:56:18,900 --> 00:56:21,880
-Don’t touch me with your dirty hands!
-Hurry and get in!

688
00:56:29,180 --> 00:56:32,080
Thank goodness.
They’ve caught the criminal.

689
00:56:32,500 --> 00:56:34,420
Is that true?

690
00:56:34,580 --> 00:56:35,700
Oh?

691
00:56:35,960 --> 00:56:37,760
Where’s Shinichi?

692
00:56:52,460 --> 00:56:54,240
As I expected…

693
00:56:54,600 --> 00:56:58,800
You are the true criminal...
Amano Shouichi.

694
00:57:00,920 --> 00:57:02,740
What do you mean by that?

695
00:57:03,140 --> 00:57:04,460
Wasn’t the criminal, Miura?

696
00:57:04,700 --> 00:57:09,920
That was a feint to root
you out as the true criminal.

697
00:57:12,060 --> 00:57:14,520
Why would I?

698
00:57:15,580 --> 00:57:18,760
I only have a few minutes
without an alibi.

699
00:57:19,620 --> 00:57:24,180
If the place of murder was here,
it’s possible that you’re the criminal.

700
00:57:26,760 --> 00:57:31,660
Karen was murdered here
and you were in trouble.

701
00:57:32,500 --> 00:57:35,640
I’ve thought of 2 reasons
why you would hang the body.

702
00:57:37,400 --> 00:57:39,980
First reason...

703
00:57:40,440 --> 00:57:43,440
To match the murder
with the threatening letter.

704
00:57:43,820 --> 00:57:48,060
Leading everyone to believe that the
person who wrote the letter is the criminal.

705
00:57:49,080 --> 00:57:52,280
And the other reason is…

706
00:57:52,620 --> 00:57:56,060
To hide the real method
behind the murder.

707
00:57:57,660 --> 00:57:59,820
The real method?

708
00:58:02,260 --> 00:58:06,620
Your goal was not to hang the body.

709
00:58:08,040 --> 00:58:11,320
But to drop the body.

710
00:58:12,000 --> 00:58:16,400
To hide the fact that the victim
had been beaten to death.

711
00:58:17,740 --> 00:58:20,600
To hide the fact that the victim
had been beaten to death?

712
00:58:32,500 --> 00:58:34,180
Stop here.

713
00:58:34,880 --> 00:58:39,360
This was the first part
which doubted me.

714
00:58:41,240 --> 00:58:43,980
Zoom in here.

715
00:58:45,780 --> 00:58:48,820
A part of hair is stuck to the head
and wasn’t dangling downwards.

716
00:58:48,960 --> 00:58:51,820
Yes it is. Why?

717
00:58:52,000 --> 00:58:53,580
It’s a bloodstain.

718
00:58:54,060 --> 00:58:55,720
There was a wound here...

719
00:58:56,000 --> 00:58:59,320
...and the blood dried
making the hair stick at this part.

720
00:58:59,680 --> 00:59:03,880
That’s why a part of her hair
wasn’t dangling downwards.

721
00:59:15,700 --> 00:59:20,900
If something falls...

722
00:59:21,280 --> 00:59:22,780
...and there’s a crack.

723
00:59:23,140 --> 00:59:29,140
People would assume that the crack
had been caused by the fall just now.

724
00:59:29,680 --> 00:59:34,300
But that crack was caused
before the fall.

725
00:59:36,000 --> 00:59:41,940
You used this illusion to hide the fact
that the victim had been beaten to death.

726
00:59:42,940 --> 00:59:47,620
Well, once forensics
examine the injury...

727
00:59:47,920 --> 00:59:52,840
...they will learn whether the wound
had been caused before or after her death.

728
00:59:53,180 --> 00:59:56,300
You had no such knowledge.

729
00:59:58,440 --> 01:00:01,420
The wound is located
on the left side of the head.

730
01:00:02,380 --> 01:00:07,140
If the victim had been beaten
to death from behind...

731
01:00:12,060 --> 01:00:14,520
What was that for!?

732
01:00:15,900 --> 01:00:18,180
The criminal is left handed.

733
01:00:19,360 --> 01:00:21,540
And you’ve just used your left hand.

734
01:00:22,160 --> 01:00:26,900
On the other hand, all the other
suspects were right handed.

735
01:00:30,360 --> 01:00:31,080
That’s messed up.

736
01:00:31,300 --> 01:00:35,640
You were forced to use
your right hand, right?

737
01:00:35,880 --> 01:00:41,200
But unknowingly, you would use
your left hand on reflex.

738
01:00:42,680 --> 01:00:44,580
Like just now.

739
01:00:50,840 --> 01:00:54,020
Just to be accused
as the criminal like that?

740
01:00:55,140 --> 01:00:58,020
You said that blood dried up
on Karen’s hair, right?

741
01:00:58,940 --> 01:01:03,980
That means Karen was killed
long before the performance started.

742
01:01:05,260 --> 01:01:07,280
I was always with the staff here.

743
01:01:07,720 --> 01:01:13,520
And at 8.45pm, Mimi and I were looking for her here.

744
01:01:14,800 --> 01:01:17,440
She was nowhere to be found by then.

745
01:01:18,360 --> 01:01:20,260
-Correct?
-Yes.

746
01:01:20,520 --> 01:01:25,060
If you say that I killed Karen here,
then where would her body be?

747
01:01:25,300 --> 01:01:27,240
It was here.

748
01:01:27,620 --> 01:01:29,580
We just couldn’t see it.

749
01:01:32,280 --> 01:01:36,040
When looking for Karen
after the incident happened.

750
01:01:36,680 --> 01:01:41,320
I came here and
had my second doubt.

751
01:01:42,300 --> 01:01:44,780
That is...

752
01:01:45,200 --> 01:01:47,800
...this amount of paint.

753
01:01:49,920 --> 01:01:53,780
<i>-She didn’t come at all?
-It’s her usual selfishness again.</i>

754
01:01:53,940 --> 01:01:57,900
At that time,
there were 3 rows of paint.

755
01:01:59,200 --> 01:02:02,920
But now 2 rows.

756
01:02:04,200 --> 01:02:05,120
What do you mean?

757
01:02:05,300 --> 01:02:09,120
They were moved back
to their original place.

758
01:02:10,860 --> 01:02:13,000
Here.

759
01:02:19,100 --> 01:02:20,980
Then what?

760
01:02:21,640 --> 01:02:26,960
You removed the paint in this box...

761
01:02:27,240 --> 01:02:31,840
...and temporarily placed
Karen’s body in here.

762
01:02:34,880 --> 01:02:38,240
A person wouldn’t fit in
such a small box.

763
01:02:38,460 --> 01:02:44,100
Among these 3 cardboard boxes,

764
01:02:47,560 --> 01:02:56,240
You move the middle one a little
further behind, to form a zig-zag.

765
01:02:57,360 --> 01:03:03,520
That is why we never thought
that they contained a body.

766
01:03:04,020 --> 01:03:08,760
When you arrange
the body in a “ku” curved shape,..

767
01:03:08,980 --> 01:03:11,320
...the body will be hidden.

768
01:03:13,080 --> 01:03:17,660
You left Karen’s body
in a “ku” curved shape,

769
01:03:19,360 --> 01:03:26,560
You took out the paint, and
covered the body with the boxes.

770
01:03:39,940 --> 01:03:42,280
It’s here.

771
01:03:43,300 --> 01:03:45,740
Karen’s blood.

772
01:03:50,120 --> 01:03:53,220
If you says so, then
show me concrete evidence!

773
01:03:53,700 --> 01:03:56,460
Concrete evidence
that says that I killed her!

774
01:03:57,720 --> 01:04:01,740
There’s one thing which
I didn’t know about earlier.

775
01:04:04,160 --> 01:04:07,260
The murder weapon
used to kill Karen.

776
01:04:09,080 --> 01:04:11,180
You shouldn’t have enough
time to dispose of it.

777
01:04:11,800 --> 01:04:15,320
But I do not know where you hid it.

778
01:04:16,840 --> 01:04:21,360
That is why I had Miura arrested…

779
01:04:21,560 --> 01:04:23,640
...to assure the true criminal
that it was safe.

780
01:04:24,320 --> 01:04:28,540
I felt that he would definitely
return to the place...

781
01:04:28,700 --> 01:04:31,780
...where he hid the murder
weapon to dispose it.

782
01:04:38,080 --> 01:04:43,340
And you fell for it.

783
01:04:58,460 --> 01:05:04,000
This is the concrete evidence.

784
01:05:12,380 --> 01:05:15,080
I didn’t mean to kill her.

785
01:05:16,820 --> 01:05:17,820
But...

786
01:05:18,160 --> 01:05:21,720
-What do you want?
-Nothing.

787
01:05:22,740 --> 01:05:25,780
-Just wanted to congratulate you.
-Lies!

788
01:05:26,600 --> 01:05:28,900
Weren’t you the one
who sent that letter?

789
01:05:29,440 --> 01:05:32,140
You were just jealous
because I was successful, right?

790
01:05:32,300 --> 01:05:36,840
Karen…
You and I loved each other.

791
01:05:37,120 --> 01:05:40,160
-And you still don’t believe me?
-I don’t believe you!

792
01:05:40,540 --> 01:05:42,280
Don’t get cocky.

793
01:05:42,540 --> 01:05:46,660
The time I spent with you is nothing
but rubbish to me now.

794
01:05:46,820 --> 01:05:49,460
No. Worse than rubbish!

795
01:05:49,700 --> 01:05:52,020
To think that
I’ve dated you disgusts me...

796
01:05:52,420 --> 01:05:54,500
...and makes me want to run away.

797
01:05:55,260 --> 01:05:58,700
Can you get out of my sight?

798
01:05:59,240 --> 01:06:01,880
Forever!

799
01:06:17,840 --> 01:06:20,540
We really believed in
one another back then.

800
01:06:22,220 --> 01:06:26,520
Even so...

801
01:06:26,820 --> 01:06:33,400
Would such feelings become nothing
more than lies after we separated?

802
01:06:38,320 --> 01:06:40,900
Shoichi Amano.

803
01:06:45,120 --> 01:06:49,180
You are under arrest for
the murder of Kotobuki Karen.

804
01:06:59,080 --> 01:07:02,580
Thank you for your assistance tonight.

805
01:07:03,460 --> 01:07:05,960
Shinichi, are you alright?

806
01:07:07,100 --> 01:07:08,580
Yes.

807
01:07:08,960 --> 01:07:14,380
Aside from that, I need you to
put her into protective custody.

808
01:07:20,340 --> 01:07:23,140
-Damn.
-Shinichi?

809
01:07:25,580 --> 01:07:28,300
-Inspector, we are ready to go.
-I’ll be there.

810
01:07:31,980 --> 01:07:35,180
That idiot. All by herself…

811
01:07:45,600 --> 01:07:49,620
If I examine all of these…

812
01:07:52,340 --> 01:07:54,320
I’m an idiot.

813
01:07:54,940 --> 01:07:58,040
I know that I don’t have much time.

814
01:08:15,060 --> 01:08:18,280
Even if I was prepared for this.

815
01:08:20,160 --> 01:08:22,200
Impossible.

816
01:08:22,320 --> 01:08:24,220
Already?

817
01:08:34,340 --> 01:08:36,820
Are you trying to act cool?

818
01:08:38,860 --> 01:08:40,500
Why?

819
01:08:41,700 --> 01:08:44,640
I’m a detective.

820
01:09:01,720 --> 01:09:03,500
Shinichi.

821
01:09:07,160 --> 01:09:08,860
It’s not what you think.

822
01:09:09,160 --> 01:09:12,760
I was targeted and scared.

823
01:09:13,800 --> 01:09:16,420
Targeted?

824
01:09:17,260 --> 01:09:19,980
Aren’t you Shinichi’s assistant?

825
01:09:20,180 --> 01:09:23,100
-Ah...no…
-You're right.

826
01:09:25,860 --> 01:09:28,000
I’m not his assistant.

827
01:09:29,000 --> 01:09:31,860
I’m a client asked him
to investigate a case for me.

828
01:09:32,340 --> 01:09:33,920
A client?

829
01:09:34,240 --> 01:09:36,340
Thanks to him the criminal
had been apprehended but...

830
01:09:36,500 --> 01:09:40,820
...the criminal’s associates who have
grudges, have come into this hotel.

831
01:09:42,420 --> 01:09:45,520
He was only trying to protect me.

832
01:09:49,980 --> 01:09:53,040
Well? Do you believe me?

833
01:09:57,780 --> 01:09:59,080
Yes.

834
01:09:59,660 --> 01:10:02,460
Anyway, let’s get out of here.

835
01:10:02,880 --> 01:10:04,760
We’ll talk later.

836
01:10:27,740 --> 01:10:30,160
Shinichi! Are you alright?

837
01:10:30,800 --> 01:10:32,820
You're strange.

838
01:10:33,280 --> 01:10:37,620
Sorry. A slight fever.

839
01:10:47,080 --> 01:10:48,680
Which one?

840
01:10:49,120 --> 01:10:53,300
<i>Up or down?
Where should I go?</i>

841
01:10:54,800 --> 01:10:57,280
I have talked to dad
about our situation just now.

842
01:10:57,560 --> 01:10:59,420
He said that he’s coming to
the rooftop on a police helicopter.

843
01:10:59,620 --> 01:11:01,520
You're fool!

844
01:11:01,760 --> 01:11:04,500
If they do that, they’ll be…

845
01:11:05,400 --> 01:11:07,640
Wait.

846
01:11:08,480 --> 01:11:10,740
That’s a good idea!

847
01:11:15,780 --> 01:11:17,220
Kudo?

848
01:11:20,540 --> 01:11:22,920
It’s the time limit.

849
01:11:25,080 --> 01:11:27,420
What do you mean?

850
01:11:33,300 --> 01:11:35,360
Get in quick!

851
01:11:38,520 --> 01:11:40,480
Shinichi, hurry!

852
01:11:41,000 --> 01:11:44,780
Sorry, Ran...

853
01:11:52,780 --> 01:11:55,760
Shinichi?

854
01:11:59,760 --> 01:12:01,140
Kudo?

855
01:12:01,580 --> 01:12:06,560
I can’t transform into Conan
in front of Ran.

856
01:12:08,700 --> 01:12:10,940
Get in quick!

857
01:12:21,480 --> 01:12:23,960
-They're here.
-Hurry up.

858
01:12:26,920 --> 01:12:30,900
If the elevator moves,
they’ll come after us.

859
01:12:32,140 --> 01:12:35,520
-I’ll stay behind and become bait.
-No!

860
01:12:35,980 --> 01:12:39,480
-We’ll leave together.
-Don’t worry.

861
01:12:41,800 --> 01:12:44,760
I...

862
01:12:45,020 --> 01:12:47,340
I can’t die yet.

863
01:12:51,940 --> 01:12:57,960
But if I do...

864
01:12:58,320 --> 01:13:03,680
...please tell Ran that...

865
01:13:04,900 --> 01:13:09,160
I will been always by her side.

866
01:13:09,680 --> 01:13:14,320
Always by her side.

867
01:13:21,940 --> 01:13:24,280
I won’t do that.

868
01:13:28,180 --> 01:13:30,580
I believe that I’ll see you again.

869
01:13:41,860 --> 01:13:44,120
Take care of Ran.

870
01:13:45,140 --> 01:13:46,840
Haibara.

871
01:13:47,020 --> 01:13:49,040
Kudo.

872
01:13:49,300 --> 01:13:51,400
See you later.

873
01:14:05,100 --> 01:14:07,100
That’s a man, Gin.

874
01:14:10,000 --> 01:14:12,460
Yes. I don’t know who he is but…

875
01:14:12,840 --> 01:14:16,020
Sherry seems to have
a knight in shining armor.

876
01:14:16,520 --> 01:14:18,760
But where is she?

877
01:14:19,140 --> 01:14:23,480
If we display his dead body...

878
01:14:23,680 --> 01:14:27,400
...Sherry will give herself out.

879
01:14:40,860 --> 01:14:43,900
I need to buy time
for them to escape.

880
01:14:53,000 --> 01:14:56,120
I need to play hide and seek
until they do.

881
01:15:00,540 --> 01:15:02,900
Where did he go?

882
01:15:20,540 --> 01:15:21,900
Damn.

883
01:15:22,080 --> 01:15:24,180
Is the helicopter there yet?

884
01:15:27,880 --> 01:15:29,520
What am I doing?

885
01:15:29,860 --> 01:15:34,020
Of course it’ll be locked.
My brain can't function properly.

886
01:15:36,540 --> 01:15:40,700
This...is the victim’s room key.

887
01:15:45,340 --> 01:15:48,100
They should have reached
the roof by now.

888
01:15:50,720 --> 01:15:52,780
It’s now or never.

889
01:16:03,760 --> 01:16:05,720
Gin.

890
01:16:09,820 --> 01:16:13,080
The knight is on the 20th floor.

891
01:16:37,400 --> 01:16:39,660
Which room should we search?

892
01:16:40,640 --> 01:16:42,380
All of them.

893
01:16:55,080 --> 01:16:56,780
He’s not here.

894
01:17:18,360 --> 01:17:20,860
It has to be this room.

895
01:17:21,440 --> 01:17:22,980
Alright.

896
01:17:31,760 --> 01:17:34,620
Give up,  Mr.Knight.

897
01:17:34,980 --> 01:17:37,580
There’s nowhere else
for you to run.

898
01:17:38,360 --> 01:17:43,700
Surrender and get on your
knees in front of my gun!

899
01:17:48,020 --> 01:17:51,220
-I wonder about that...
-What?

900
01:17:54,300 --> 01:17:55,580
Damn. No lights.

901
01:17:55,780 --> 01:17:59,440
Can you hear this sound?

902
01:18:01,660 --> 01:18:03,520
I called them.

903
01:18:04,160 --> 01:18:08,680
It’s the sound of 20 helicopters
from the police SWAT team.

904
01:18:09,220 --> 01:18:10,820
What?

905
01:18:17,100 --> 01:18:22,560
They’re over there!
I’m coming for you, Ran!

906
01:18:31,000 --> 01:18:32,260
What?!

907
01:18:32,440 --> 01:18:36,400
According to Ran, there should be
Ran, the boy detective and his client.

908
01:18:36,580 --> 01:18:39,120
Isn’t that the professor’s kid?

909
01:18:39,460 --> 01:18:41,980
The detective brother is being
chased down by bad men.

910
01:18:42,160 --> 01:18:44,040
Save him! Hurry!

911
01:18:44,200 --> 01:18:45,840
Boy Detective?

912
01:18:46,140 --> 01:18:48,440
Where! Where is he?

913
01:18:51,580 --> 01:18:56,500
Soon, there’ll be about 50 officers
rushing down towards here.

914
01:18:59,800 --> 01:19:04,580
You guys should be
the ones surrendering.

915
01:19:04,740 --> 01:19:07,500
-Gin.
-Don’t buy into it.

916
01:19:08,040 --> 01:19:09,700
It’s a bluff.

917
01:19:10,400 --> 01:19:12,520
If that were true...

918
01:19:12,680 --> 01:19:16,580
...they should have come here directly
when we heard the helicopter sounds.

919
01:19:18,260 --> 01:19:20,000
That’s most likely...

920
01:19:20,720 --> 01:19:23,520
...the TV station’s helicopter...

921
01:19:23,860 --> 01:19:26,160
...which came to film the party.

922
01:19:26,900 --> 01:19:28,460
There you are.

923
01:19:30,360 --> 01:19:32,600
What are you?

924
01:19:33,920 --> 01:19:36,520
You...?

925
01:19:36,960 --> 01:19:38,860
A detective.

926
01:19:48,420 --> 01:19:51,360
There he is! Boy detective!

927
01:19:53,820 --> 01:19:55,800
It’s the cops!

928
01:20:31,360 --> 01:20:34,680
-Boy detective!
-Kudo!

929
01:20:50,820 --> 01:20:53,200
Ran, do you recognize me?

930
01:20:54,540 --> 01:20:55,900
Dad?

931
01:20:56,500 --> 01:20:58,720
Thank goodness.

932
01:20:59,720 --> 01:21:03,060
Ran!
You worried us.

933
01:21:05,260 --> 01:21:08,360
Ai, why are you here?

934
01:21:09,080 --> 01:21:13,220
She said that she got lost in the
building and ended up on the rooftop.

935
01:21:13,560 --> 01:21:15,760
Hairi who was holding you...

936
01:21:16,000 --> 01:21:19,440
...left you with Ai and
returned into the building.

937
01:21:20,760 --> 01:21:25,020
She told Ai that a police helicopter
would arrive and everything would be fine.

938
01:21:26,080 --> 01:21:28,040
I see…

939
01:21:29,940 --> 01:21:32,000
Shinchi?

940
01:21:37,260 --> 01:21:39,120
Where’s Shinichi?

941
01:21:40,260 --> 01:21:44,880
-Kudo is on to another case…
-He’s dead.

942
01:21:46,960 --> 01:21:48,660
Eh?

943
01:21:50,700 --> 01:21:53,860
That good for nothing is dead.

944
01:21:55,520 --> 01:21:58,040
He’s dead.

945
01:21:59,160 --> 01:22:01,240
Impossible.

946
01:22:01,640 --> 01:22:03,800
He was lying, right?

947
01:22:14,320 --> 01:22:18,620
No. I can’t be.

948
01:22:20,580 --> 01:22:25,660
I believed that he’ll come back.

949
01:22:26,480 --> 01:22:28,780
I believed...

950
01:22:31,400 --> 01:22:33,360
It’s ringing.

951
01:22:35,740 --> 01:22:38,540
Your phone’s ringing.

952
01:22:42,840 --> 01:22:45,180
Shinchi?
Shinchi, is that you?

953
01:22:45,620 --> 01:22:47,940
You know it’s me.

954
01:22:48,500 --> 01:22:51,740
Thank goodness.
You're alive.

955
01:22:53,660 --> 01:22:56,460
Idiot. Idiot!

956
01:22:57,640 --> 01:22:58,760
How?!

957
01:22:59,000 --> 01:23:02,540
-That explosion just now…
-No way!

958
01:23:02,780 --> 01:23:05,260
I’m fine. You don’t have
to call me an idiot.

959
01:23:07,920 --> 01:23:12,640
Idiot. Idiot. Idiot....

960
01:23:13,220 --> 01:23:16,560
You…

961
01:23:17,100 --> 01:23:20,420
Hairi, is she safe?

962
01:23:22,900 --> 01:23:25,260
Y...Yes...

963
01:23:25,700 --> 01:23:27,560
She’s fine.

964
01:23:27,900 --> 01:23:30,780
Her pursuers got spooked
by the police and ran.

965
01:23:31,820 --> 01:23:35,200
I want to see you, Shinichi.

966
01:23:36,160 --> 01:23:38,340
I want to see you now.

967
01:23:38,700 --> 01:23:39,840
Sorry…

968
01:23:40,080 --> 01:23:44,640
After I take her to somewhere safe,
I have another case.

969
01:23:45,300 --> 01:23:47,620
I still have a lot to do.

970
01:23:47,920 --> 01:23:49,600
Don’t worry.

971
01:23:49,880 --> 01:23:53,820
I’ll come back someday...

972
01:23:54,020 --> 01:23:56,120
...just to see your silly face.

973
01:23:57,980 --> 01:24:00,100
The ”silly” part is unnecessary.

974
01:24:00,740 --> 01:24:03,400
If the professor is there,
let me talk to him.

975
01:24:03,820 --> 01:24:06,100
I have something to ask from him.

976
01:24:08,440 --> 01:24:10,180
It's a call from Shinichi.

977
01:24:11,920 --> 01:24:14,460
Hello...Hello?

978
01:24:14,720 --> 01:24:18,700
You’re really lucky.
How did you survive?

979
01:24:19,220 --> 01:24:24,460
I have to thank Suzuki Conglomerate
for building that laundry chute box.

980
01:24:25,420 --> 01:24:29,640
Just before the explosion, I transformed
back into Conan and used it to escape.

981
01:24:34,740 --> 01:24:36,060
I see.

982
01:24:36,280 --> 01:24:41,520
And...can you bring me my kiddy
clothes? I have nothing to wear.

983
01:24:41,760 --> 01:24:44,380
Sorry. But can you ask
the professor directly?

984
01:24:44,760 --> 01:24:47,500
I don’t feel want to see you in the nude.

985
01:24:50,900 --> 01:24:52,820
Hey! Haibara!

986
01:24:53,040 --> 01:24:55,380
Don’t just snatch the phone
and hang up like that.

987
01:24:55,560 --> 01:24:57,980
Think what I went through all
that trouble to save you.

988
01:24:59,920 --> 01:25:03,500
There was only 1 police helicopter.

989
01:25:04,120 --> 01:25:06,700
They must have after receiving
a report about a building robbery.

990
01:25:07,900 --> 01:25:10,700
-That was a bluff after all.
-Yes.

991
01:25:11,360 --> 01:25:13,700
I snooped around
the hotel again but...

992
01:25:13,880 --> 01:25:15,640
...that woman was
nowhere to be found.

993
01:25:16,120 --> 01:25:18,660
And that helicopter was gone too.

994
01:25:20,440 --> 01:25:26,840
Even so, who was that man
whom he blew up?

995
01:25:27,900 --> 01:25:29,460
A detective.

996
01:25:38,700 --> 01:25:40,900
Could it be?

997
01:25:45,160 --> 01:25:48,440
But dad, how did you know
which room Shinichi was in?

998
01:25:49,920 --> 01:25:54,760
Well it is because of the Great Detective
Kogoro Mori’s great skills of reasoning.

999
01:25:55,020 --> 01:25:56,760
How did you know?

1000
01:25:57,760 --> 01:26:01,900
That hotel used lighting
to form a message.

1001
01:26:02,860 --> 01:26:05,800
The “Suzu” word from
Suzuki Congromerate’s name...

1002
01:26:06,200 --> 01:26:09,520
But there was one room
without the lights on.

1003
01:26:10,360 --> 01:26:16,600
And that is the room where I thought
that detective boy was hiding.

1004
01:26:17,140 --> 01:26:20,320
Wow! As expected of dad.

1005
01:26:20,780 --> 01:26:22,900
Today, I’ll make whatever you like.

1006
01:26:23,200 --> 01:26:25,480
Well...Well...
Can I have 5 bottles of beer?

1007
01:26:25,780 --> 01:26:27,100
No, you can’t.

1008
01:26:29,280 --> 01:26:32,000
-I’m back.
-You're late.

1009
01:26:32,420 --> 01:26:34,400
Even after leaving early,
where were you?

1010
01:26:34,580 --> 01:26:39,960
The professor’s place. He bought
a new game and I was hooked unto it.

1011
01:26:40,120 --> 01:26:42,780
I see. I was worried.

1012
01:26:50,540 --> 01:26:53,700
Sister Ran.
Did something good happen?

1013
01:26:55,000 --> 01:26:57,640
I met Shinichi today.

1014
01:26:58,000 --> 01:27:01,080
-Brother Shinichi?
-Yes.

1015
01:27:05,740 --> 01:27:07,600
What a beautiful full moon.

1016
01:27:07,980 --> 01:27:10,600
Come, Conan.

1017
01:27:14,440 --> 01:27:18,380
Is Shinichi looking at it
from somewhere, too?

1018
01:27:21,300 --> 01:27:25,000
He probably tired
and sleeping by now.

1019
01:27:47,420 --> 01:27:51,440
I’m watching it with you...

1020
01:27:51,960 --> 01:27:54,020
Ran...

